                <pb facs="0806" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">791.003/83</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Embassy to the
                            Department of State</hi></head>
                <p>We are very glad to co-operate with the United States in Persia. The Chargé
                    d’Affaires of Italy at Teheran has been instructed to keep himself in touch with
                    the American Representative. Italy, too, excludes the possibility of the system
                    of Capitulations being maintained and is of the opinion that all interested
                    Countries should act of one accord as to the guarantees to be requested. It is
                    unfortunate that, so far, it has been impossible to come to an understanding,
                    especially on account of the attitude of the French Government which has
                    preferred to act singly. An extension of the treaty is evidently desirable, but
                    in view of the present disposition of the Persian Government, it hardly seems
                    that it can be obtained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1928-03-15"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">March 15, 1928</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
